Falsifies `system_tests::user::futex_tests::the_reserved_futex_forms_and_foreign_words_are_refused`.

Architecture: aarch64, riscv64, x86_64

The defect: the futex methods of milestone 812 (`std::thread::spawn` runs real threads in one
address space) admit every flags word, so a shared futex and a 64-bit futex, both of which §269
(how threads share a process) reserves, are served as if they were the private 32-bit form.

Expected to fail: "a shared futex was not refused as a form this kernel does not answer", which
gets `NotPermitted` from the next check instead of `BadMethod`.

diff --git a/crates/abi/src/lib.rs b/crates/abi/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/abi/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/abi/src/lib.rs
@@ -1114,7 +1114,8 @@ pub mod futex {
 
     /// **Is this a `flags` word the kernel answers?** Exactly one today.
     pub const fn admitted(flags: u64) -> bool {
-        flags == PRIVATE | SIZE_U32
+        let _ = flags;
+        true
     }
 }
 
